 "about": "A mine's pithead on a rock over a drop, 42 by 28 m, the same for red (-x) and blue (+x) turned about its middle, on three floors. The yard (y 0) in the middle, open to the sky, the sword on a stepped dais under the gantry; a headframe at each end, its hall at the foot with doors to the yard, the arcade and the spur, its mezzanine (y 3.5) up the west wall, its crown (y 7) up the same wall or by the skip lift from the yard. The gantry (y 7) runs crown to crown over the yard, the sniper in its middle. Along each long side a deck (y 3.5) from one team's mezzanine to a ramp down to the other's spur, an arcade under it on the yard; the overshield out at the north deck's edge, the camo at the south's. The spurs, the decks' edges and the gantry's sides are open: off the rock is death. Out of the rotation until it has been played.",
